From 16a10d7b1f4444bc02f3cb514ab107c3fba8eeed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:46:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ppc64le: turn the DFG on

The DFG tier needs no ppc64le backend of its own: DFGSpeculativeJIT64.cpp is
generic over the MacroAssembler, which this port has and which the Baseline
tier already exercises. It was off because it had never been measured, and the
comment here said FTL and the DFG both "need B3/Air lowering that does not
exist" -- that lowering exists now.

Measured over JSTests/stress, 5833 tests: a DFG build fails 34, and all 34
fail identically with --useDFGJIT=false, checked one at a time. So the DFG
introduces no failure that the Baseline tier does not already have. Two bugs
that did show up were fixed in WebKit first -- an upstream UB cast in
operationStringFromCodePointUntyped, and and32/or32/xor32 not honouring Air's
ZDef contract, which was also corrupting array indices through `^`.

Worth about 3.2x: a 40M-iteration integer loop 2639ms -> 818ms, an
object/float workload 854ms -> 288ms, against node 26's 653ms and 152ms.

FTL stays off. Not for want of a backend -- testb3 is 998/1000 and FTL builds,
tiers up and returns correct answers -- but because the same suite still shows
79 failures to the DFG build's 34. Enabling it also drags in BBQ and OMG
through WEBKIT_OPTION_DEPEND, and those need a vector layer in
MacroAssemblerPPC64.h that is not written.
---
 scripts/build/deps/webkit.ts | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/build/deps/webkit.ts b/scripts/build/deps/webkit.ts
index 936c9624920..135ead73500 100644
--- a/scripts/build/deps/webkit.ts
+++ b/scripts/build/deps/webkit.ts
@@ -336,14 +336,28 @@ export const webkit: Dependency = {
       // generated LLIntAssembly.h rather than the flags we passed, so a WebKit
       // without that branch fails loudly instead of silently building a CLoop.
       //
-      // ENABLE_DFG_JIT stays explicit: nothing defaults it off, and ENABLE_JIT
-      // with the DFG off is a configuration nobody else builds. FTL needs the
-      // B3/Air lowering that does not exist, which is also what keeps
-      // WEBKIT_OPTION_DEPEND from turning BBQ and OMG on — wasm is IPInt-only.
-      // ENABLE_YARR_JIT is decided inside PlatformEnable.h.
+      // ENABLE_DFG_JIT is ON. The DFG has no per-target backend to write --
+      // DFGSpeculativeJIT64.cpp is generic over the MacroAssembler, which this
+      // port has -- and it is now measured clean: across JSTests/stress (5833
+      // tests) a DFG build fails 34, and every one of those 34 fails
+      // identically with --useDFGJIT=false, so the DFG introduces nothing.
+      // Worth roughly 3.2x: a 40M-iteration integer loop goes 2639ms -> 818ms
+      // and an object/float workload 854ms -> 288ms, against node 26's 653ms
+      // and 152ms on the same box.
+      //
+      // FTL stays OFF, and no longer because the Air backend is missing -- it
+      // is here, testb3 is 998/1000, and FTL builds and runs. It is off
+      // because it is not clean yet: the same suite shows 79 failures against
+      // the DFG build's 34, so something like 25-60 FTL-specific ones remain
+      // (two runs of one binary differ by 18 tests, so a single figure would
+      // be false precision). WEBKIT_OPTION_DEPEND ties BBQ and OMG to FTL, so
+      // wasm stays IPInt-only with it off -- and those two additionally need a
+      // vector layer in MacroAssemblerPPC64.h that does not exist.
+      //
+      // ENABLE_YARR_JIT is decided inside PlatformEnable.h, and is ON.
       ...(cfg.ppc64le
         ? {
-            ENABLE_DFG_JIT: "OFF",
+            ENABLE_DFG_JIT: "ON",
             ENABLE_SAMPLING_PROFILER: "ON",
             // The cmake branch above defaults this off too, but bun's own
             // USE_MIMALLOC below is conditional on !asan, and the two must not
